    <summary>Local voice to text software that types speech at the cursor of any Windows app and turns audio or video recordings into .txt files without sending them to a server.</summary>
    <description>SayOnce - Voice to Text Software is voice to text software that lets staff dictate into any Windows application instead of typing, with recognition done on the PC itself. For IT teams deploying it with Chocolatey across an office, a clinic or a support desk, the main point is that recorded speech is not uploaded anywhere for transcription.

![SayOnce - Voice Dictation Software screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/vds/vds-v1-dictate.png)

## How to use it

1. Install the package and start the program once on each PC so it can download its speech model (about 478 MB).
2. Click into an email, a form, a document or a chat.
3. Press and hold Ctrl+Win, say the text, then let go.
4. The words are pasted at the cursor. Choose Prose, Code or Email on the main screen to change formatting.
5. To turn meetings or interviews into notes, add audio or video files on the Files tab.

&gt; Trial note: the free trial runs without a day limit but caps the number of dictations per day, after which the hotkey is blocked. A license lifts the cap.

![SayOnce - Voice Dictation Software screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/vds/vds-v1-presets.png)

## What the package puts on a PC

- The desktop app with a tray icon and an overlay that shows listening and processing states.
- Settings for the microphone, hotkey, push-to-talk, paste method, autostart and app language.
- A speech model kept on the local disk after the first download, which can be unloaded from memory after a set idle time.
- Batch transcription to .txt, saved next to each source file or in one output folder.

Snippets replace a short spoken phrase with a stored block of text, such as an address or a sign-off, and the personal dictionary helps it get names and terms used in your team right.

## Who it is for

- Office staff who write many emails and fill in forms.
- Medical staff entering patient notes between appointments.
- Developers dictating instructions into an IDE.
- Teams that turn recorded lectures, webinars and interviews into text.

![SayOnce - Voice Dictation Software screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/vds/vds-v1-settings.png)

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of SayOnce, commercial voice to text software by SoftOrbits. Full use without the daily dictation limit requires a paid license, and activating it may need an internet connection. Plans and volume discounts: [voice dictation software for Windows](https://www.softorbits.net/voice-dictation-software/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package).

[SayOnce - Voice to Text Software on Windows Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9PLMH8G96XLR)

## FAQ

### Is there a free speech-to-text?

The free trial of this speech to text software keeps every feature but has a daily dictation limit. A license removes that limit.

### What makes a dictation program for PC worth installing?

It should work in the programs you already use, respond quickly and keep audio private. SayOnce pastes into any active window and runs recognition locally, and a graphics card is not required.

### Which tool should I use for converting speech to text?

For live typing, a hotkey tool that pastes at the cursor fits best. For recordings, you need a file transcriber that outputs text. This voice typing software covers both, through dictation and the Files tab.
